=== tip 40610
To get server information
Press "refresh" button to retrieve the list 
of servers started at the moment. 
Note that your computer must be connected 
to the Internet.

=== tip 40611
Add/remove server in the address book 
For your convenience you can bookmark a server in your address book. 
These servers will be always in the list (they are marked yellow). 
Add server to the address book: pressing the "Add/remove" button 
calls up the window to enter/edit the server address. In case one of the 
active servers has been selected from the list at the moment, its address 
will appear in the window. 
Remove server: choose a server from the address book and press the
"add/remove" button.

=== tip 40612
Private server 
Open server is being registered in the list of active servers available to all 
players. To start an open server the player must have access to the Internet. 
A private server is one on a local network, and players are not required 
to have access to the Internet. 
Note that players can join a private server from the Internet only if 
they have its IP address, and if the server is connected to the Internet.

